+## 0j. Session 13: Apple HIG pass on Windows, macOS and Linux (⚠️ not run in a real desktop window)
+The user asked for the HIG review items 1, 2, 3, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13 and 14 (4: one sidebar instead of rail + list, and 5: system accent instead of per-page petals, were left out on purpose). Mid-session they asked for every change to apply to Windows and Linux too, with Mac-only behaviour adapted, and for the full-width **New Chat** button to come back.
+Verified here: `tsc` clean · `vite build` OK · all earlier suites pass (63 base, 34 builder, 56/24 s5, 27/11 s7, 22 s10, 12 s11, 3 s12; 5 render expectations updated for renamed labels, listed below) · **10 new session 13 tests** (`run-s13-tests.sh`) · Chromium screenshots (`shoot-s13.mjs`, light and dark) checked by eye, with these scripted checks: Ctrl+F focuses the page search, deleting a chat then pressing Undo restores it, Esc closes Settings. No Rust changed.
+- **Alerts and Undo (1):** `components/common/Alerts.tsx`. `window.confirm` is gone: model and voice-model deletes use an in-app alert with the app icon, a title naming the item, Cancel on the leading side and **Delete** as the default. Deleting a conversation or an image generation no longer happens at once: the item hides, a "… deleted · Undo" note shows for 8 s at the top of the window, and the delete runs when the note closes (or on leaving the page or quitting). Edit › Undo / Ctrl+Z takes it back when the cursor is not in a text field. ⚠️ On the Mac, ⌘Z goes to the system Undo item, so only the note's Undo button restores the item there.
+- **Menus (2), every OS:** File gains New Image, New Project…, New Task (`lib/commands.ts` hands the command to the page, even if it hasn't mounted yet). Edit gains Find… (Ctrl/⌘F focuses the page's search field). View: Show/Hide Sidebar and Show/Hide Inspector (Windows/Linux Ctrl+Alt+S / I; Mac ⌃⌘S / ⌥⌘I), Library…, Plugins…, Enter Full Screen (F11 on Windows/Linux; macOS adds its own). Appearance left the View menu (it stays in Settings). New **Go** menu: Back/Forward (Alt+←/→; Mac ⌘[ / ⌘]) and the pages (Ctrl/⌘1–6). Help: Lotus Help (F1; ⌘?) opens the README. On Windows/Linux one key handler now serves every menu shortcut. On the Mac the native menu handles them (no double toggles); Close Window, Full Screen and Bring All to Front come from the system; Window and Help are registered with macOS (window list, Help search).
+- **AI output (3):** the latest reply always shows Copy, Try Again, Good reply and Bad reply (older ones on hover). Feedback is stored on the message (`feedback`, `feedbackNote`). With memory on and skills used, a thumbs-up counts a skill win and a thumbs-down rewrites the skill (`chat/feedback.ts`). Placeholders name the model ("qwen3:8b is reading your message…"), and "Working…/Loading…/Generating…" were made specific. An empty chat offers four starter prompts that fill the box, plus a line saying local models can make mistakes.
+- **Engine status (6):** every "X isn't running at http://…" banner became one quiet line with a grey dot and a **Start Ollama / Start ComfyUI / Start Voicebox** button. It shows Open Engines when Lotus can't start the engine here (remote, ComfyUI path unknown, failed start). The line sits next to what it blocks, e.g. above the chat box (`components/common/EngineNotice.tsx`, `EnginesContext` from App).
+- **New buttons (7):** Images and Voice use a compose icon next to the sidebar search. **Chat keeps its full-width New Chat button** (user's request). Labels are Title Case.
+- **Settings (8):** a pane toolbar with icons and short names (Models, Engines, Chat, Memory, Voice, Island, Appearance, Updates, Legal). The title is the pane's name and there is no Done button (Esc or the close button closes; the close button is on the left on the Mac). It reopens on the last pane (`lotus.settingsPane.v1`), and Help › Check for Updates… opens on Updates. Appearance keeps Auto as the default.
+- **Polish (9–14):** truncated labels fixed (chat inspector "Parameters" → "Model", Settings pane names, font picker wider). Every button label is Title Case. ALL-CAPS section headers are gone. `cursor-pointer` was removed (no hand cursor on buttons). Kanban columns are separated by thin lines instead of grey boxes. The petal colour dots in Settings › Appearance became a plain sentence. 11 px and 10 px text became 12 px (the island and citation superscripts excepted). Cross-platform copy: "this PC" → "this computer"; Show in Explorer / Finder / Files by OS; the microphone-blocked message names the right settings app per OS.
+- **Stale test expectations updated (with evidence):** "Choose folder" → "Choose Folder", "Send answers" → "Send Answers", "Import plugin file" → "Import Plugin File", "New chat" → "New Chat" (builder tray), Tasks offline text, title-bar toggles renamed sidebar/inspector. The old "no sidebar toggle" absence check now checks that the old "left/right panel" names are gone.
